(iii) the well documented flaws in the federal environmental assessment process, including flawed surveys of the iconic Black Cockatoo, and* >> >> *(iv) the failure of the Government to release key documents to inform public evaluation of this project; and* > > *(b) calls on the Minister representing the Minister for Infrastructure and Regional Development:* > >> *(i) to reprioritise $925 million in federal funding allocated to this project to actual solutions to Perth's freight task, including investment in freight rail and the Outer Harbour, and* >> >> *(ii) to urgently request That the federal assessment be delayed until such time as the judicial review in the Supreme Court has been completed.*","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-3937","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2015-10-12/4"}
